              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Some people think that children should not be allowed to use smartphones until they are teenagers. To what extent do you agree or disagree?",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Introdução:",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "It is often suggested that young children should be kept away from smartphones until their teenage years. I largely agree with this view, as early smartphone use can harm both children's concentration and their social development.",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Body 1 (PEEL):",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "(P) The main reason why I support this idea is that smartphones can seriously reduce children's ability to concentrate. (E) Apps and games are designed to give instant rewards, which makes slower activities, such as reading or homework, seem boring in comparison. (E) For instance, many primary school teachers report that pupils who spend hours on devices find it difficult to focus during lessons. (L) Therefore, limiting access to smartphones would help children develop the attention they need to learn.",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Body 2:",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "(P) A further argument is that face-to-face play is essential for developing social skills. …",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
